    "sha": "9c08b726f5d13057f8319dbbc4001a58dc4d2604",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDljMDhiNzI2ZjVkMTMwNTdmODMxOWRiYmM0MDAxYTU4ZGM0ZDI2MDQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T02:33:54Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T02:58:42Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(slot): a Slot takes a start point and an exit point\n\nA start pick chooses the slot end where the pass starts. An exit pick\nchooses the end where it stops. A pick only swaps the two ends of the\nslot: slot(b, a) is slot(a, b) turned half a turn, so no new move shape\nis made. A pick that the pass cannot hold is refused by name: out of\nreach of the cutter path, the same distance from both ends, an exit at\nan end where the row count does not stop the pass, a tilted slot.\n\nWithout a pick the ends come back as they are, so each earlier slot is\nthe same to the byte. The other kinds of #3325 stay refused by name.\n\nThe Slot's Lead in / Lead out tab draws the Start point and Exit point\ngroups, and the viewport pick takes the Slot.\n\nRefs #3325\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
